{"parentUuid":"e6c6ab9c-3714-4cb0-ba5e-81d78eab45d6","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.493Z","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019t91ptjpEiua6WQ5fB6Jvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pzt5mgW2hPxw8UFbvPWUiA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/qwrr-layer.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_read_input_tokens":58731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYaZWujkwY18d8UB18Viv","uuid":"0983d6d2-5163-4efa-9b9f-f6521a0f5e52"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"5ef9efd9-2dd1-456d-a356-868ec85e380f","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.495Z"}
{"parentUuid":"5ef9efd9-2dd1-456d-a356-868ec85e380f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pzt5mgW2hPxw8UFbvPWUiA","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Rhea — Quota Walls, Relays, and Resurrection\n     2→*Extended “fancy-bonused” spec for surviving provider caps without replacing a Claude-shaped brain.*\n     3→\n     4→> Situation: Rex (Claude-shaped routing judgment) can become unavailable behind provider quota walls.  \n     5→> Goal: Keep the office moving with **guaranteed delivery, no loss, no duplicates, no zombie side-effects**, and clean resumption when Rex wakes.\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## 0) Executive Summary (for people who hate reading)\n    10→- **Do not “replace Rex’s brain”** with a different model and pretend it’s equivalent.\n    11→- **Do build a persistent relay + resurrection timer** that buffers messages, guarantees delivery, and drains in-order when Rex returns.\n    12→- Make relay bank-grade by adding: **seq ordering**, **idempotency keys**, **lease/fencing gates**, **TTL/deadline**, **staleness checks**, and **receipts**.\n    13→\n    14→---\n    15→\n    16→## 1) Why the “brain on different hardware” shortcut fails\n    17→**Truth:** model behavior is part of the agent’s identity.  \n    18→Routing judgment is **Claude-shaped**. A Gemini proxy won’t route the same way, even if you paste “persona”.\n    19→\n    20→### What *can* be portable\n    21→- **State packs** (what is true)\n    22→- **Policy packs** (what is allowed)\n    23→- **Tool packs** (what can be executed)\n    24→- **Transport mechanics** (how messages get delivered)\n    25→\n    26→### What is not portable without changing the agent\n    27→- “judgment style” / routing heuristics / refusal boundaries / latent preferences\n    28→\n    29→> Bonus: Stop thinking of “agent identity” as a prompt. Treat it as `State + Policy + Tools + (Model-specific cognition)`.\n    30→\n    31→---\n    32→\n    33→## 2) The right “different angle”: Relay + Resurrection Timer\n    34→### Design intent\n    35→- Rex is down → messages accumulate safely (durable mailbox)\n    36→- Rex wakes → messages are delivered exactly once in-order\n    37→- Side-effects occur only under valid lease/fencing token (“STOP means STOP”)\n    38→\n    39→### Minimum components\n    40→1) **Mailbox Store** (durable, ordered)\n    41→2) **Delivery Worker** (retries + acks)\n    42→3) **Resurrection Timer** (availability watcher)\n    43→4) **Rex boot protocol** (catch-up → drain mailbox → gated effects)\n    44→5) **Receipts + incidents** (proof of termination and accountability)\n    45→\n    46→---\n    47→\n    48→## 3) Bank-grade invariants (falsifiable)\n    49→These must be testable under chaos (kill -9, reconnects, duplicates).\n    50→\n    51→### I1 — No message loss\n    52→Every outbound command to Rex becomes a mailbox record first.\n    53→\n    54→### I2 — In-order delivery per runpoint\n    55→Messages have `seq` monotonic per `runpoint_id` (or a robust cursor scheme).\n    56→\n    57→### I3 — Exactly-once *processing* (or exactly-once effects)\n    58→At minimum, processing is at-least-once but **idempotent**.\n    59→For side-effects: exactly-once via **intent + receipt**.\n    60→\n    61→### I4 — STOP semantics survive downtime\n    62→If STOP is issued while Rex is down, Rex cannot “catch up and execute” old effects blindly.\n    63→\n    64→### I5 — No zombie effects\n    65→Old Rex instance must not be able to push commits/write critical state after lease revocation.\n    66→\n    67→---\n    68→\n    69→## 4) Message Envelope (required fields)\n    70→Every mailbox message MUST include an envelope that supports:\n    71→- idempotency\n    72→- ordering\n    73→- schema evolution\n    74→- gating by lease token\n    75→- auditability\n    76→\n    77→### Envelope v1\n    78→```json\n    79→{\n    80→  \"id\": \"uuidv7\",\n    81→  \"runpoint_id\": \"rp_...\",\n    82→  \"seq\": 12345,\n    83→  \"type\": \"msg.send | task.create | decision.record | effect.request | ...\",\n    84→  \"timestamp\": \"2026-02-17T12:00:00Z\",\n    85→  \"source\": \"Argos|B2|GPT|LEAD|Human\",\n    86→  \"target\": \"Rex\",\n    87→  \"version\": 1,\n    88→  \"lease_token_required\": 991, \n    89→  \"idempotency_key\": \"string\",\n    90→  \"ttl_s\": 86400,\n    91→  \"payload\": { \"...\" }\n    92→}\n    93→\n    94→Rules:\n    95→\t•\tseq is monotonic within runpoint_id\n    96→\t•\tidempotency_key is stable across retries\n    97→\t•\tttl_s + timestamp define expiry\n    98→\t•\tlease_token_required must match current lease token for any dangerous operation\n    99→\n   100→Bonus: include prev_hash/hash for tamper-evidence if you treat mailbox as part of your audit trail.\n   101→\n   102→⸻\n   103→\n   104→5) Firestore-backed Relay Layout (Google-scope friendly)\n   105→\n   106→Collections (recommended)\n   107→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/mailbox/{agent_id}/messages/{message_id}\n   108→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/acks/{agent_id}/{message_id}\n   109→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/leases/{agent_id}\n   110→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/snapshots/{agent_id}\n   111→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/incidents/{incident_id}\n   112→\t•\trunpoints/{runpoint_id}/effect_intents/{intent_id}\n   113→\n   114→Indexing must support:\n   115→\t•\tfetch messages ordered by seq\n   116→\t•\tfetch undelivered messages where status != acked (or missing ack)\n   117→\t•\tquery by time window for expiry cleanup\n   118→\n   119→Note: Firestore listeners are a convenience. Catch-up must work by querying seq > last_seq_applied.\n   120→\n   121→⸻\n   122→\n   123→6) Delivery worker (relay daemon) — deterministic algorithm\n   124→\n   125→Enqueue (producer side)\n   126→\t1.\tValidate envelope (no secrets, schema ok)\n   127→\t2.\tWrite message to mailbox (durable)\n   128→\t3.\tOptionally emit an EVENT_ENQUEUED event for observability\n   129→\n   130→Deliver (consumer side)\n   131→\n   132→For each runpoint/agent:\n   133→\t1.\tRead last_seq_acked (or reconstruct from acks)\n   134→\t2.\tFetch mailbox messages seq > last_seq_acked ordered, limited batch\n   135→\t3.\tFor each message:\n   136→\t•\tif expired → mark expired, emit incident, continue\n   137→\t•\tattempt delivery to target agent’s inbox endpoint\n   138→\t•\ton success → write ack doc (idempotent upsert)\n   139→\t•\ton failure → retry with exponential backoff + jitter\n   140→\t4.\tPeriodically garbage-collect old acked messages\n   141→\n   142→Ack semantics (idempotent)\n   143→\n   144→Ack doc write must be safe to repeat:\n   145→\t•\tacks/{message_id} is created once; further writes are no-ops.\n   146→\n   147→Bonus: If you store the delivery_attempts counter and last_error, you get debugging for free.\n   148→\n   149→⸻\n   150→\n   151→7) Resurrection Timer — dumb by design\n   152→\n   153→Timer does not route, reason, or “help”. It only:\n   154→\t•\tchecks whether Rex is reachable/alive\n   155→\t•\ttriggers the relay to drain mailbox when Rex returns\n   156→\n   157→Availability check\n   158→\t•\theartbeat events or a simple health endpoint\n   159→\t•\tor Firestore presence document updated by Rex\n   160→\n   161→Wake sequence\n   162→\t•\t“Rex is alive” → relay switches from “queue-only” to “drain mode”\n   163→\n   164→⸻\n   165→\n   166→8) Rex boot protocol (the crucial “no loss, no staleness” sequence)\n   167→\n   168→When Rex starts (or restarts):\n   169→\t1.\tAcquire lease (monotonic lease_token)\n   170→\t2.\tLoad snapshot (last_seq_applied, state_hash, capsule)\n   171→\t3.\tCatch up by querying events/messages with seq > last_seq_applied to latest\n   172→\t4.\tOnly after catch-up: drain mailbox in-order\n   173→\t5.\tBefore any side-effect:\n   174→\t•\tverify lease token still current\n   175→\t•\tenforce TTL/staleness policy\n   176→\t•\tconvert to effect intent if needed (outbox pattern)\n   177→\t6.\tCommit new snapshot and update heartbeat\n   178→\n   179→Staleness policy (must exist):\n   180→\t•\ttask.create can be executed after delay\n   181→\t•\teffect.request may require re-confirmation if age > threshold\n   182→\t•\tpush now must expire or require “fresh approve” event\n   183→\n   184→Bonus: This makes your system safe under long downtimes instead of “execute everything when back online”.\n   185→\n   186→⸻\n   187→\n   188→9) Side-effects: effect intents + receipts (no double pushes)\n   189→\n   190→Never let mailbox messages directly do “dangerous” actions.\n   191→They should create effect intents.\n   192→\n   193→Effect intent record\n   194→\n   195→{\n   196→  \"intent_id\": \"uuidv7\",\n   197→  \"runpoint_id\": \"rp_...\",\n   198→  \"kind\": \"git_commit|git_push|firestore_write|http_call\",\n   199→  \"idempotency_key\": \"same-as-message-or-derived\",\n   200→  \"lease_token\": 991,\n   201→  \"payload\": { \"...\" },\n   202→  \"status\": \"planned|sent|committed|failed\",\n   203→  \"receipt\": { \"commit_sha\": \"...\", \"response_hash\": \"...\"},\n   204→  \"created_at\": \"...\",\n   205→  \"updated_at\": \"...\"\n   206→}\n   207→\n   208→Executor rules:\n   209→\t•\treject intents with stale lease_token\n   210→\t•\tdedupe on idempotency_key\n   211→\t•\twrite receipts\n   212→\n   213→Bonus: This is where you get “termination proof artifacts”.\n   214→\n   215→⸻\n   216→\n   217→10) Fancy bonuses (worth selling, worth community hype)\n   218→\n   219→B1 — “Quota wall immunity”\n   220→\n   221→Provider caps stop being outages; they become a logged degraded mode:\n   222→\t•\tsystem keeps queuing work and resumes safely\n   223→\n   224→B2 — “Time travel”\n   225→\n   226→Because everything is sequenced and replayable:\n   227→\t•\tyou can replay the last week/month for debugging\n   228→\t•\tcompare “what Rex would have done” vs “what proxy did”\n   229→\n   230→B3 — “Transparent accountability”\n   231→\n   232→Community gets:\n   233→\t•\treceipts for outcomes\n   234→\t•\tincident reports when things expire or get stuck\n   235→\t•\taudit trail for decisions\n   236→\n   237→B4 — “Human-free mediation”\n   238→\n   239→You’re no longer the courier between AIs:\n   240→\t•\teveryone writes to the same relay bus\n   241→\t•\tRex drains when available\n   242→\n   243→B5 — “Safe multi-runpoint expansion”\n   244→\n   245→Same relay pattern supports:\n   246→\t•\tmultiple personal runpoints\n   247→\t•\tstrict isolation by runpoint_id\n   248→\n   249→B6 — “Policy-driven staleness”\n   250→\n   251→You can define:\n   252→\t•\twhich messages may execute late\n   253→\t•\twhich require re-approval\n   254→This avoids “surprise execution after downtime”.\n   255→\n   256→B7 — “Commercial leverage”\n   257→\n   258→You can sell this as:\n   259→\t•\t“resilient agent ops”\n   260→\t•\t“audit-grade multi-model office”\n   261→\t•\t“recoverable research pipelines”\n   262→\n   263→⸻\n   264→\n   265→11) Acceptance tests (must pass)\n   266→\n   267→T1 — Rex down 12h\n   268→\t•\tmessages queued\n   269→\t•\tno loss\n   270→\t•\ton wake: delivered once in order\n   271→\n   272→T2 — Duplicate delivery attempts\n   273→\t•\tretries happen\n   274→\t•\tonly one ack exists\n   275→\t•\tprocessing idempotent, no duplicated side-effects\n   276→\n   277→T3 — STOP issued during downtime\n   278→\t•\tSTOP event prevents dangerous intents post-wake\n   279→\t•\tlease token gating blocks stale execution\n   280→\n   281→T4 — Split-brain (two Rex processes)\n   282→\t•\tonly current lease token can commit intents\n   283→\t•\tstale Rex cannot push anything\n   284→\n   285→T5 — Expiry/staleness\n   286→\t•\tlate “push now” expires and logs incident\n   287→\t•\tlate “task.create” still executes (if allowed)\n   288→\n   289→⸻\n   290→\n   291→12) Implementation roadmap (minimal pain)\n   292→\n   293→Phase 0 (today)\n   294→\t•\tdefine envelope v1\n   295→\t•\timplement mailbox writes + ack docs\n   296→\t•\timplement drain logic by seq\n   297→\n   298→Phase 1 (this week)\n   299→\t•\tleases + fencing token\n   300→\t•\tstaleness/TTL policy\n   301→\t•\tincidents for expired/stuck messages\n   302→\n   303→Phase 2\n   304→\t•\teffect intents + receipts executor\n   305→\t•\tdeterministic snapshots + state_hash\n   306→\t•\tchaos tests\n   307→\n   308→Phase 3\n   309→\t•\tfancy cockpit UI for relay state\n   310→\t•\treplay tooling + analytics\n   311→\n   312→⸻\n   313→\n   314→13) Don’t do these (common self-owns)\n   315→\t•\tDo not store “truth” in browser extension localStorage\n   316→\t•\tDo not rely on Firestore listener as the only mechanism (catch-up must exist)\n   317→\t•\tDo not allow mailbox messages to directly perform side-effects\n   318→\t•\tDo not skip lease/fencing (zombie worker will bite you)\n   319→\n   320→⸻\n   321→\n   322→14) Resulting posture\n   323→\n   324→With relay + resurrection + leases + intents:\n   325→\t•\tquota walls become a delay, not a system failure\n   326→\t•\trestarting agents is safe and routine\n   327→\t•\thumans stop being couriers between models\n   328→\t•\tyou get auditability and proof artifacts worthy of “bank-grade”\n   329→\n   330→If you want an even more “product-grade” version, I can generate a companion `relay_api.md` that lists exact endpoints/tools for Office and for a future MCP gateway (inputs/outputs/error codes) — but this file above already captures the operational backbone and the sellable “bonuses.”"}]},"uuid":"0fae7f4e-de24-4902-914e-8dceefdace93","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.949Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"355e7084-1551-4d4c-b293-8ce8efa957af","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.971Z"}
{"parentUuid":"355e7084-1551-4d4c-b293-8ce8efa957af","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.973Z","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019t91ptjpEiua6WQ5fB6Jvc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017G8EEY3kgBjGn6tdCt2GxP","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/procedures/rhea-radio.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_read_input_tokens":58731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYaZWujkwY18d8UB18Viv","uuid":"05573fd2-9cb8-444e-9b84-7050962f52af"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"bbdb280a-0a0f-4c49-963e-8ada3f65782f","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:13.976Z"}
{"parentUuid":"bbdb280a-0a0f-4c49-963e-8ada3f65782f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017G8EEY3kgBjGn6tdCt2GxP","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# RHEA Radio\n     2→\n     3→Date: 2026-02-28  \n     4→Owner: ORION  \n     5→Status: ACTIVE\n     6→\n     7→## Objective\n     8→Duplicate agent work signals into a continuous local \"radio\" channel:\n     9→- live feed log\n    10→- macOS notifications\n    11→\n    12→This is the operator-facing frequency for ongoing work visibility.\n    13→\n    14→## Commands\n    15→```bash\n    16→bash scripts/rhea.sh radio start --interval 2\n    17→bash scripts/rhea.sh radio status\n    18→bash scripts/rhea.sh radio tail 40\n    19→bash scripts/rhea.sh radio listen\n    20→bash scripts/rhea.sh radio stop\n    21→\n    22→# NDI/screen-capture watchdog (feeds radio)\n    23→bash scripts/rhea.sh ndi start --interval 6\n    24→bash scripts/rhea.sh ndi status\n    25→bash scripts/rhea.sh ndi tail 40\n    26→bash scripts/rhea.sh ndi stop\n    27→\n    28→# Queue/log overflow maintainer + UI applet\n    29→bash scripts/rhea.sh queue start --interval 30\n    30→bash scripts/rhea.sh queue status\n    31→bash scripts/rhea.sh queue compact\n    32→bash scripts/rhea.sh queue-applet\n    33→```\n    34→\n    35→## Signal Sources\n    36→- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_mailbox.jsonl`\n    37→- `opera/ops/virtual-office/relay_acks.jsonl`\n    38→- `logs/bridge_calls.jsonl`\n    39→- `opera/tasks/queue.jsonl`\n    40→- `opera/metrics/ndi_trace.jsonl`\n    41→- `opera/metrics/queue_guard_trace.jsonl`\n    42→\n    43→## Artifacts\n    44→- Feed: `opera/metrics/radio_feed.jsonl`\n    45→- Pulse: `opera/metrics/radio_pulse.json`\n    46→- State: `.rhea/radio/state.json`\n    47→- Daemon stdout: `.rhea/radio/radio.stdout.log`\n    48→- NDI pulse: `opera/metrics/ndi_pulse.json`\n    49→- Queue health pulse: `opera/metrics/queue_health.json`\n    50→- Compact archives: `opera/metrics/compact/*.jsonl.gz`\n    51→\n    52→## Behavior\n    53→- High-signal events notify by default (P0/P1 relay, bridge errors, task add/claim/complete/blocked).\n    54→- Dedup cooldown prevents duplicate spam.\n    55→- Full event stream is always appended to feed log.\n    56→- Every ~30s, radio writes a lossy-compressed `radio_pulse.json` health summary.\n    57→- Queue guard trims overflowing logs and archives old lines as gzip for compact retention.\n    58→\n    59→## Rule\n    60→For operator-critical workflows, radio stays ON during active work blocks.\n    61→"}]},"uuid":"4100ba9c-1a61-49ac-b281-243b3aef1611","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:14.120Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"Search the codebase for any references to \"atomicmail\", \"atomic mail\", \"rhea mailbox\", or email-related mailbox configuration. Check opera/ops/, docs/, and src/ directories. Also check CLAUDE.md files and any configuration files. Report what you find about Rhea's mailbox system.","agentId":"a9bb77653714893ac"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_01S6nKLoVA64hvGxYuSQXUTq","parentToolUseID":"toolu_01JZFNKKYAqziLSrvyqrn7F3","uuid":"268c3ee7-ba2e-4e7d-aa71-0fad9f8ba9ea","timestamp":"2026-02-28T13:40:14.421Z"}
