{"parentUuid":"bcb8963b-6859-4431-a787-3c5172458bb3","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LpVacdiUUy7LjhDXjXeHS8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Build 1.0 (5) uploaded successfully.** App Store Connect is processing it now.\n\nThe archive is also in Xcode Organizer now — you should see a 5th entry with version `1.0 (5)` if you refresh. This one has:\n- App icon (1024x1024 with the \"R\" logo)\n- All 4 iPad orientations\n- `CFBundleIconName: AppIcon`\n- Proper version from build settings (no more hardcoded \"1\")\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nxcodegen's `info.properties` writes literal values into Info.plist by default. To make `MARKETING_VERSION` and `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` from build settings work, you must explicitly set `CFBundleShortVersionString: $(MARKETING_VERSION)` and `CFBundleVersion: $(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION)` in the properties. Without this, the plist gets hardcoded \"1.0\" and \"1\" regardless of what the build settings say — which is why all 4 archives showed `1.0 (1)`.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_read_input_tokens":125263,"output_tokens":287,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CYacJUqa9E6A5HR1EobX4","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9b6ddac-1df7-4497-8518-fecd614ae884","timestamp":"2026-02-28T14:16:53.360Z"}
