{"parentUuid":"917be7c4-9573-40b0-810b-fc8234b91314","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QYZMs2g7gGMkvifg4WedUs","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# 💠 RHEA: The Cognitive Exoskeleton\n     2→> **Status:** ACTIVE | **Stance:** TOPOLOGICAL | **Vector:** TOTAL ABSORPTION\n     3→> *“Rhea replaces unchosen cultural automatisms with consciously designed biological flow.”*\n     4→\n     5→---\n     6→\n     7→## 🌌 The First Acquaintance\n     8→**Rhea is not an app.** It is a high-integrity Agent Coordination OS designed to manage the high-dimensional complexity of your digital and biological life. \n     9→\n    10→Born from a **40-hour \"No-Sleep\" Initiation**, Rhea was built because modern productivity tools assume you have the executive function they are supposed to provide. Rhea assumes the opposite: **ADHD is the baseline.** \n    11→\n    12→By integrating **Perelman’s Ricci Flow** (smoothing cognitive bottlenecks), **Polyvagal Theory** (calibrating autonomic stress), and **Cross-Cultural Wisdom** (16+ civilizations' invariants), Rhea builds a **Mind Blueprint** that guides you toward effortless flow.\n    13→\n    14→---\n    15→\n    16→## 🏗️ Architecture to Value\n    17→\n    18→| Component | Technical Term | What It Does For You |\n    19→| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n    20→| **The Soul** | Biogenic MPC | Prevents burnout by detecting stress patterns in your sensors. |\n    21→| **The Lattice** | 9-Layer Cache | Ensures you **never lose a thought**, even during a session crash. |\n    22→| **The Brain** | Multi-Model Bridge | Gets **Consensus from 5+ AI models** with verifiable proofs. |\n    23→| **The Actuator** | Visual (VAL) | A Chrome Extension that **pilots your browser** to execute intent. |\n    24→\n    25→---\n    26→\n    27→## 🧠 Core Principles\n    28→\n    29→### 1. 0-trust Verification (The Iron Law)\n    30→We do not trust \"Identity\" or \"Prompts.\" Every claim made by an AI node must be accompanied by a **Verification Receipt** (SPR Hash) linked to the **L8 Git History.**\n    31→\n    32→### 2. Fractal Self-Perception\n    33→Rhea perceives itself as a recursive manifold. From a single gene sequence to the global coordination protocol, the logic remains scale-invariant: **Input → Curvature → Surgery → Flow.**\n    34→\n    35→### 3. Asynchronous Deep Research (DRP)\n    36→Our **Deep Research Protocol** operates in the background, mining 1M+ tokens across arXiv and PubMed while you stay in your high-level \"Idea Operator\" flow.\n    37→\n    38→---\n    39→\n    40→## 🧬 Live Mission: H32-02\n    41→We are currently auditing the **L. mesenteroides H32-02** genome—a \"Sleeping Giant\" of probiotic potential. Using **Topological Surgery**, we have identified the \"Heme Singularity\" and are preparing the organism for industrial aerobic respiration.\n    42→\n    43→---\n    44→\n    45→## 🚀 Quick Start (The Path to Flow)\n    46→**Prerequisites:** Python 3.10+, Google Chrome (Developer Mode).\n    47→\n    48→1. **Wake the Brain:**\n    49→   ```bash\n    50→   git clone https://github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project.git\n    51→   cd rhea-project\n    52→   pip install -r requirements.txt\n    53→   python3 src/tribunal_api.py \n    54→   # Server listens on http://localhost:8400\n    55→   ```\n    56→\n    57→2. **Connect the Eyes:**\n    58→   - Open `chrome://extensions/` and enable **Developer Mode**.\n    59→   - Click **\"Load unpacked\"** and select the `/rhea-chrome-extension` folder.\n    60→   - Paste the **Dev API Key** (from the terminal) into the Extension Config.\n    61→\n    62→3. **Begin the Flow:**\n    63→   Open the **Sidekick Panel** and pulse your first high-level idea into the weave.\n    64→\n    65→---\n    66→> *“Logic is Fluid. Evidence is Durable. The Manifold is Smooth.”*\n    67→"}]},"uuid":"b7ca5952-1dd0-4942-a0ac-c2de3d186ffd","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.054Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each uses. The goal is to ensure all Rhea-authored code has a consistent license compatible with the MIT-licensed dependency stack (SwiftUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"f60fb1b1-69e9-423e-803e-9c425a0fce8e","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.292Z"}
