{"parentUuid":"bfe0b997-97df-49eb-bc8b-d0e2025c68e6","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017tcDXNwkeaDKasiA5d31HS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# friends/\n     2→\n     3→Referenced traditions that Rhea absorbs with respect. Independent, equal, honored.\n     4→\n     5→## aletheia/\n     6→Greek -- \"un-concealment.\" Truth as the act of revealing what was hidden.\n     7→Parmenides, Heidegger. Contains: hypotheses, proofs, community science output.\n     8→\n     9→## ruliad/\n    10→Wolfram's Ruliad -- the entangled limit of all possible computations.\n    11→Contains: ontology explorer, multi-perspective sampling, source references.\n    12→\n    13→Both traditions contribute to Rhea's exploration. Neither owns this space. Rhea does.\n    14→We are all in the same ontology boat.\n    15→"}]},"uuid":"550201f4-d40c-4667-9e52-e46a3523cbe1","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.333Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each