tUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"4df75d0a-d371-4b5c-94e5-b7800404bfbc","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.640Z"}
{"parentUuid":"4df75d0a-d371-4b5c-94e5-b7800404bfbc","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UJNMzHvtgSb7WxxLNPsXYw","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# RHEA ATLAS UI (The Glass)\n     2→> Version: 8.0 | License: Sovereign Logic | Influence: LobeUI / Linear\n     3→\n     4→## 1. Overview\n     5→The Rhea Atlas is a high-density logical observer built with **Next.js 14**, **React Three Fiber**, and **Framer Motion**. It is designed to visualize the **Ruliadic Manifold** and provide a \"Scientific Jewelry\" interface for high-stakes research.\n     6→\n     7→## 2. Design Tokens\n     8→- **Primary Background:** `#050505` (Deep Obsidian)\n     9→- **Accent Color:** `#00FFFF` (Cyan Logic)\n    10→- **Glassmorphism:** `backdrop-blur-xl` + `border-white/10`\n    11→- **Typography:** `Geist Sans` (Vercel) for headers, `Geist Mono` for logical data.\n    12→\n    13→## 3. Core Components\n    14→### `<RuliadicIsland />`\n    15→The primary unit of knowledge.\n    16→- **Props:** `position`, `color`, `complexity (D-Metric)`, `onClick`.\n    17→- **Interaction:** Pulses on logic-events; clickable for Interrogation.\n    18→\n    19→### `<MagneticNebula />`\n    20→The background substrate. Reacts to cursor movement via Magnetic Field Shaders.\n    21→\n    22→### `<CouncilTheatre />` (Coming Soon)\n    23→A high-end panel for parallel Tribunal streams.\n    24→\n    25→## 4. Extensibility (The Plugin Hook)\n    26→To add a new visualization layer, register a component in `src/components/plugins/`. All plugins must accept the `RelayChain` stream via the `useAtlasStore`.\n    27→\n    28→## 5. Development\n    29→```bash\n    30→cd rhea-atlas\n    31→npm run dev\n    32→```\n    33→"}]},"uuid":"75bee35d-bdb7-4fa3-8e05-fcb0f9cb36c1","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.695Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each uses. The goal is to ensure all Rhea-authored code has a consistent license compatible with the MIT-licensed dependency stack (SwiftUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"180e06b2-65b1-4c40-b51d-220b68ef81da","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:25:11.698Z"}
