{"parentUuid":"dda79b77-5d59-4514-8ab2-63606c4c1882","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VMDGq6JFAwuP9bcemstBpf","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Terms of Service\n     2→\n     3→**Rhea Research Platform**\n     4→TimeLabs NPO\n     5→Last updated: 2026-02-26\n     6→\n     7→---\n     8→\n     9→## 1. Acceptance\n    10→\n    11→By accessing or using the Rhea platform, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the platform.\n    12→\n    13→Rhea is operated by **TimeLabs NPO**, a non-profit organization focused on scientific research in chronobiology and related disciplines.\n    14→\n    15→---\n    16→\n    17→## 2. What Rhea Is\n    18→\n    19→Rhea is a multi-model AI advisory system designed to assist researchers, scientists, and curious individuals. It is a **research tool**, not a medical device, clinical instrument, or licensed professional service.\n    20→\n    21→Outputs from Rhea are **informational only**. They do not constitute medical advice, legal advice, financial advice, or any other regulated professional guidance.\n    22→\n    23→---\n    24→\n    25→## 3. Permitted Use\n    26→\n    27→You may use Rhea to:\n    28→- Conduct scientific research and analysis\n    29→- Explore hypotheses in chronobiology, pharmacology, and adjacent fields\n    30→- Query AI models for literature synthesis, protocol design, and data interpretation\n    31→- Share outputs for academic, educational, or non-commercial purposes\n    32→\n    33→**Fair use is expected.** You agree not to:\n    34→- Use Rhea to generate disinformation, harassment, or harmful content\n    35→- Attempt to reverse-engineer, scrape, or abuse the platform's infrastructure\n    36→- Violate any applicable local, national, or international law\n    37→- Impersonate researchers, institutions, or other users\n    38→- Use automated bots or scripts against the platform without written permission\n    39→\n    40→---\n    41→\n    42→## 4. No Warranties\n    43→\n    44→Rhea is provided **\"as is\"** and **\"as available\"**.\n    45→\n    46→TimeLabs NPO makes no warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to:\n    47→- Accuracy or completeness of AI-generated content\n    48→- Fitness for any particular scientific or clinical purpose\n    49→- Uninterrupted or error-free availability\n    50→- Compatibility with your systems or workflows\n    51→\n    52→AI models can hallucinate, make errors, or produce outdated information. Always verify outputs against authoritative sources. **Do not rely on Rhea outputs for clinical or safety-critical decisions.**\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→## 5. Limitation of Liability\n    57→\n    58→To the maximum extent permitted by law, TimeLabs NPO and its contributors shall not be liable for:\n    59→- Any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from platform use\n    60→- Errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in AI-generated content\n    61→- Decisions made based on platform outputs\n    62→- Data loss, service interruption, or unauthorized access events\n    63→\n    64→---\n    65→\n    66→## 6. Intellectual Property\n    67→\n    68→- **Your inputs and research**: remain yours. TimeLabs NPO does not claim ownership of queries you submit.\n    69→- **Platform code**: open source under the license in the GitHub repository (github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project).\n    70→- **AI model outputs**: governed by the terms of the underlying model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.).\n    71→\n    72→---\n    73→\n    74→## 7. Open Source and Contributions\n    75→\n    76→Rhea's source code is publicly available at **github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project**. Contributions are welcome under the repository's contributing guidelines. By submitting a pull request or contribution, you agree that your contribution may be incorporated under the project's open-source license.\n    77→\n    78→---\n    79→\n    80→## 8. Accounts and Access\n    81→\n    82→If Rhea offers account creation in the future:\n    83→- You are responsible for maintaining the security of your credentials\n    84→- You must not share accounts or allow unauthorized access\n    85→- TimeLabs NPO reserves the right to suspend accounts that violate these Terms\n    86→\n    87→---\n    88→\n    89→## 9. Changes to These Terms\n    90→\n    91→TimeLabs NPO may update these Terms. Changes will be posted in this file with an updated date and noted in the repository changelog. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.\n    92→\n    93→---\n    94→\n    95→## 10. Governing Law\n    96→\n    97→These Terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction where TimeLabs NPO is established. Disputes shall be resolved in good faith first; escalation proceeds under applicable law.\n    98→\n    99→---\n   100→\n   101→## 11. Contact\n   102→\n   103→Questions about these Terms:\n   104→**celestica201@gmail.com**\n   105→GitHub: github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project\n   106→"}]},"uuid":"8a933c67-d86e-424f-8b9d-aa7ef9d40fd2","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:12.746Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each uses. The goal is to ensure all Rhea-authored code has a consistent license compatible with the MIT-licensed dependency stack (SwiftUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"103199a2-edf7-40f7-801e-627ac4534169","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:12.752Z"}
