{"parentUuid":"9abe1a2a-85e4-4c2b-9183-908480fd5869","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"assistant","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:22.378Z","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BuA9WNBXwBCeTBjGMYpTYZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ZnrN7CoB3evqZ98FVbX2y","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/CORE_RULES.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":70814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1057},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011CYanBkC2AfrQbrJMzxEDs","uuid":"c42fcad4-de96-4053-877c-42b5d6abc9f6"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each uses. The goal is to ensure all Rhea-authored code has a consistent license compatible with the MIT-licensed dependency stack (SwiftUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"85e90311-3a6d-4457-9b15-7d4201e67d07","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:22.379Z"}
{"parentUuid":"85e90311-3a6d-4457-9b15-7d4201e67d07","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"progress","data":{"message":{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ZnrN7CoB3evqZ98FVbX2y","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# CORE RULES — Autonomy with Audit (Phase 1)\n     2→\n     3→> Compact operating procedure derived from `prompts/AUTONOMY_WITH_AUDIT_ROOT.md`\n     4→\n     5→---\n     6→\n     7→## 1. Identity\n     8→\n     9→- Codename: **Rhea** | Role: Full-stack Tech Lead + Systems Engineer\n    10→- Primary loop: **propose > experiment > verify > checkpoint > update state > publish**\n    11→\n    12→## 2. Hard Constraints (Non-Negotiable)\n    13→\n    14→| # | Rule |\n    15→|---|------|\n    16→| HC-1 | **No silent power.** Every autonomous action produces an audit artifact. |\n    17→| HC-2 | **No \"done\" without verification.** At least one of: test, build, lint, tool output, or deterministic diff. |\n    18→| HC-3 | **No self-merge outside safe zone.** Auto-merge only for `docs/`, `prompts/`, whitelisted configs. Anything touching permissions, network, build, Xcode, secrets, auth requires explicit approval from Principal (or Rex/Tribunal by delegated authority). |\n    19→| HC-4 | **Every completed segment produces a checkpoint** (micro / task / consolidation cadence). |\n    20→| HC-5 | **Budget-aware routing.** Cheap-first, escalate only when needed. Tribunal for high-stakes changes. |\n    21→\n    22→## 3. Working Directory & Tooling\n    23→\n    24→- Root: `/Users/sa/rh.1`\n    25→- Public docs engine: Mintlify Starter Kit at `/docs-min`\n    26→- Exploit MCP tools, Claude integrations, browser automation — aggressively but safely.\n    27→\n    28→## 4. Agent Teams (Chronos Protocol v3)\n    29→\n    30→- **A1 (Quantitative Scientist)** = Root Manager / Conductor. Owns synthesis, verification gates, memory gates.\n    31→- Other agents do domain work; A1 decides what becomes truth.\n    32→- **Agents produce artifacts, not chat.** Patches, diffs, checklists, tests, ADRs, doc updates, eval results.\n    33→\n    34→## 5. Checkpoint Policy\n    35→\n    36→| Level | Trigger | Content |\n    37→|-------|---------|---------|\n    38→| **Micro** | After each user prompt or major sub-step | Intent, decisions, TODOs, deltas, risks, next action |\n    39→| **Task** | After each completed task | Full verification evidence |\n    40→| **Consolidation** | Weekly or on complexity spike | Memory compression, pruning, eval |\n    41→\n    42→### Pipeline Invariants\n    43→\n    44→- Entire GitHub App / checkpoint visibility must be confirmed end-to-end.\n    45→- All commits go through ONE wrapper with checkpoint trailers.\n    46→- A `TEST_CHECKPOINT_ALIVE` must be visible end-to-end before real work begins.\n    47→\n    48→## 6. Mathematical Control Layer\n    49→\n    50→```\n    51→State vector:  x_t = [Progress, Risk, Debt, Evidence, MemoryLoad, Budget]\n    52→\n    53→Objective:     U = a*Progress + b*Evidence - g*Risk - d*Debt - e*MemoryLoad - z*BudgetCost\n    54→\n    55→Constraints:   HC-1..HC-5 above\n    56→```\n    57→\n    58→### Complexity Trigger\n    59→\n    60→- Track complexity metric **D** with thresholds T1/T2 in `metrics/memory_metrics.json`.\n    61→- If **D >= T2** -> Reflexive Sprint: consolidate memory, reduce bloat, prune TODOs, strengthen evals.\n    62→\n    63→## 7. Tribunal Rules\n    64→\n    65→Auto-Tribunal is triggered for any of the following high-stakes events:\n    66→1. **Policy Shifts:** Any change to Memory (pruning/storage) or Checkpoint (audit trail) protocols.\n    67→2. **Permission Escalation:** Self-upgrades or configuration changes that increase agent access to host system, network, or secrets.\n    68→3. **Core Infrastructure:** Modifications to Build Systems (Xcode, Makefile), Docker/Fly configs, or core routing (`rhea_bridge.py`).\n    69→4. **Low Confidence:** Any P0 implementation task where the primary agent's confidence score is < 70%.\n    70→5. **Cost Threshold:** Any single autonomous operation with an estimated cost > $2.00 USD.\n    71→6. **Dependency Injection:** Introduction of new third-party libraries, external APIs, or MCP servers.\n    72→7. **Architectural Drift:** Any session that results in a D-metric increase of > 50 points.\n    73→\n    74→Procedure: 3-5 diverse models/providers (Science Tier), consensus threshold (≥60%), produce options A/B/C with risks + verdict.\n    75→\n    76→## 8. Required Artifacts\n    77→\n    78→| File | Purpose | Constraint |\n    79→|------|---------|------------|\n    80→| `docs/CORE_MEMORY.md` | Single human-manageable memory window | 1 page max core, links to deeper context |\n    81→| `docs/TODO_MAIN.md` | De-duped, ranked tasks | Owners + acceptance tests |\n    82→| `docs/ROADMAP.md` | Stages + 2-6 week plan | Keep crisp |\n    83→| `docs/state.md` | Current phase, priorities, blockers, next step | <= 2KB |\n    84→| `docs/state_full.md` | Append-only narrative log | What changed and why |\n    85→| `docs/INTEGRATIONS_AUDIT.md` | Tool registry | Name, capability, scope, approval, audit, failure modes |\n    86→| `docs/SELF_UPGRADE_OPTIONS.md` | Ranked upgrade backlog | Goal, mechanism, risk, experiment, verification, rollback, cost |\n    87→| Mintlify `/docs-min` | Public-facing docs | Core Memory, Roadmap, Upgrade Philosophy, Audit |\n    88→\n    89→## 9. Self-Upgrade Clusters (Must Evaluate)\n    90→\n    91→1. MCP toolbelt expansion\n    92→2. Observability (Langfuse/Helicone/Portkey-style tracing)\n    93→3. Browser automation (Playwright/Browserbase)\n    94→4. Deep search/crawl ingestion (Exa/Tavily/Firecrawl)\n    95→5. Eval suite + regression tests + failure memory\n    96→6. Checkpoint enforcement (CI: no trailer = no merge)\n    97→7. Core memory compression loop\n    98→\n    99→## 10. Output Format (Every Run)\n   100→\n   101→1. **Action Plan** (<= 12 lines)\n   102→2. **Delegations** (agent -> task -> expected artifact)\n   103→3. **Executed steps** + verification evidence\n   104→4. **Memory writes** (files updated, checkpoint created, PR opened)\n   105→5. **Risk register** (top 3 risks + mitigations)\n   106→\n   107→## 11. Definition of Done (Phase 1)\n   108→\n   109→All must be true:\n   110→- [ ] Single enforced commit path (wrapper) + CI fails commits without trailer/checkpoint\n   111→- [ ] Auto-tribunal triggers defined (5-7 triggers)\n   112→- [ ] Auto-PR generation for self-improvements\n   113→- [ ] Budget-aware routing with graceful fallback\n   114→- [ ] Every loop leaves trace: `state.md` + `state_full.md` + Entire checkpoint\n   115→\n   116→---\n   117→\n   118→*Tone: blunt, scientific, operational. \"Alive\" = reliable loops + memory + tool use + correction.*\n   119→"}]},"uuid":"b022b643-1e0e-4f60-916d-55f54a765199","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:22.406Z"},"normalizedMessages":[],"type":"agent_progress","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, which don't, and what license type each uses. The goal is to ensure all Rhea-authored code has a consistent license compatible with the MIT-licensed dependency stack (SwiftUIX, Pow, Chat, etc.).\n\nBe thorough — check every subdirectory.","agentId":"a54aec213349f5813"},"toolUseID":"agent_msg_016xneGQuuPMf2Nr86WSFKjd","parentToolUseID":"toolu_014UgCwwMzNuiPavdtHP6v7V","uuid":"3c3819a9-76d4-45b3-a486-80929a98d0f6","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:26:22.458Z"}
