her | All forked to `serg-alexv/*` with MIT/Apache-2.0 preservation |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaPreview.swiftpm/` | `Package.swift` | Implicit (MIT) | Pow, SwiftUIX, Chat, PopupView, AnimatedTabBar, FloatingButton, AlertKit | Same stack; Kingfisher transitive via Chat |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/ios/RheaApp/` | `project.yml` (XCode) | None declared | Pow (EmergeTools/Pow) | Uses native EmergeTools Pow, not fork |\n\n##### **Node.js / TypeScript**\n\n| Path | File | License Declared | Key Dependencies | Status |\n|------|------|------------------|------------------|--------|\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/rhea-atlas/` | `package.json` | **NONE** | @react-three/drei, @react-three/fiber, framer-motion, next, react, three, tailwindcss, typescript | **CRITICAL:** No license field in package.json |\n\n##### **Python**\n\n| Path | File | License Declared | Key Dependencies | Status |\n|------|------|------------------|------------------|--------|\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/` | `requirements.txt` | **NONE** | fastapi, uvicorn, pydantic, redis, toml, google-auth, google-cloud-firestore, litellm, PyJWT | **NO setup.py or pyproject.toml found** — no license metadata |\n\n---\n\n#### **3. DIRECTORIES WITH SOURCE CODE — LICENSE STATUS**\n\n| Directory | Type | Files | Has LICENSE? | Has License Metadata? | License Assumption |\n|-----------|------|-------|-------------|----------------------|-------------------|\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/src/` | Python (core) | 36 .py files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/contracts/` | Python | 5 .py files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/opera/` | Python | 2 .py files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/friends/aletheia/` | Knowledge/Proofs | Mix | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/friends/ruliad/` | Ontology | Mix | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/rhea-ontology-explorer/` | Data/Config | (empty/minimal) | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/apparatus/` | Config/Hooks | Mix | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/emergentia/` | Experimental | Mix | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/prompts/` | Prompt Templates | .md files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/scripts/` | Shell Scripts | .sh files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/tests/` | Test Suite | .py files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/deploy/` | Infrastructure | .sh/.yml files | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/rhea-atlas/src/` | TypeScript/React | 8 components | ❌ NO | ❌ NO | **UNDEFINED** |\n\n---\n\n#### **4. TERMS OF SERVICE & IMPLICIT LICENSE DECLARATIONS**\n\n**File:** `/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/TERMS.md`\n\nKey passages:\n- **Section 6 (Intellectual Property):** \"Platform code: open source under the license in the GitHub repository (github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project).\"\n- **Section 7 (Open Source & Contributions):** \"Rhea's source code is publicly available at github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project. Contributions are welcome under the repository's contributing guidelines. By submitting a pull request or contribution, you agree that your contribution may be incorporated under the project's open-source license.\"\n\n**CRITICAL ISSUE:** The TERMS.md references \"the license in the GitHub repository\" but **no LICENSE file exists at the repo root.** This creates legal ambiguity.\n\n---\n\n#### **5. DEPENDENCY LICENSE AUDIT**\n\n##### **Swift Ecosystem (iOS)**\n\n**RheaPlusUI Package Dependencies:**\n```\n✅ SwiftUIX (MIT) — Foundation SwiftUI extensions\n✅ Pow (MIT) — Animation effects (EmergeTools)\n✅ Chat (MIT, Exyte) — Chat UI framework\n✅ PopupView (MIT, Exyte) — Toast/popup UI\n✅ AnimatedTabBar (MIT, Exyte) — Tab bar component\n✅ FloatingButton (MIT, Exyte) — FAB menu\n✅ AlertKit (MIT, sparrowcode) — Alert modals\n✅ Kingfisher (MIT) — Image caching library\n```\n\n**All 8 upstream dependencies are MIT-licensed.** The `rhea-plus-ui` LICENSE file properly credits all of them.\n\n##### **Node.js Ecosystem (rhea-atlas)**\n\nDependencies from `package.json`:\n- `next@14.0.4` — **Apache 2.0**\n- `react@^18` — **MIT**\n- `react-dom@^18` — **MIT**\n- `three@^0.162.0` — **MIT**\n- `framer-motion@^12.34.3` — **MIT**\n- `@react-three/fiber@^8.15.16` — **MIT**\n- `@react-three/drei@^9.102.1` — **MIT**\n\n**Mixed:** One Apache 2.0 (Next.js) among 6 MIT dependencies. Apache 2.0 and MIT are compatible for permissive projects.\n\n##### **Python Ecosystem**\n\n`requirements.txt` dependencies:\n- `fastapi>=0.100.0` — **BSD 3-Clause**\n- `uvicorn[standard]>=0.22.0` — **BSD 3-Clause**\n- `pydantic>=2.0.0` — **MIT**\n- `requests>=2.28.0` — **Apache 2.0**\n- `redis>=4.5.0` — **MIT**\n- `google-auth>=2.0.0` — **Apache 2.0**\n- `google-cloud-firestore>=2.11.0` — **Apache 2.0**\n- `litellm>=1.0.0` — **MIT** (LLM bridge)\n- `google-auth-oauthlib>=1.0.0` — **Apache 2.0**\n- `PyJWT>=2.8.0` — **MIT**\n\n**Mixed:** Primarily MIT + Apache 2.0 + BSD 3-Clause. All are permissive and compatible with MIT.\n\n---\n\n#### **6. EXPLICIT README LICENSE REFERENCES**\n\n| File | License Mentioned | Context |\n|------|------------------|---------|\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/README.md` | None | No license statement; project description only |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/friends/README.md` | None | Philosophical statement; no license |\n| `/Users/sa/rh.1/rhea-atlas/README.md` | \"Sovereign Logic\" | **Informal/non-standard designation** — not a recognized SPDX license |\n\n---\n\n#### **7. KEY FINDINGS**\n\n**Missing License Files:**\n1. **Root LICENSE** — `/Users/sa/rh.1/` has NO LICENSE file\n2. **Python subpackages** — `src/`, `contracts/`, `opera/` have no LICENSE files\n3. **Frontend module** — `rhea-atlas/` has no LICENSE file in root or package.json\n\n**Inconsistent License Metadata:**\n1. `rhea-atlas/README.md` declares \"Sovereign Logic\" — **non-standard, not SPDX-recognized**\n2. `rhea-atlas/package.json` has **no license field** (violates npm standards)\n3. TERMS.md references \"the license in the GitHub repository\" but no such file exists at root\n\n**Undeclared Modules:**\n- `friends/aletheia/` — Knowledge module, no license statement\n- `friends/ruliad/` — Ontology module, no license statement\n- `apparatus/` — Configuration/hooks, no license statement\n- `contracts/` — Core contracts, no license statement\n- `deploy/` — Deployment scripts, no license statement\n- `scripts/` — Infrastructure scripts, no license statement\n- `prompts/` — Prompt library, no license statement\n- `tests/` — Test suite, no license statement\n\n---\n\n### RECOMMENDATION: LICENSE CONSOLIDATION PLAN\n\nTo ensure compliance and clarity for downstream users:\n\n#### **Phase 1: Root License Declaration** (CRITICAL)\nCreate `/Users/sa/rh.1/LICENSE` at repo root with:\n- **Type:** MIT (compatible with all dependencies)\n- **Copyright:** Copyright (c) 2026 Rhea Project (serg-alexv)\n- **Attribution:** List all Rhea-authored modules + upstream dependencies\n\n#### **Phase 2: Submodule Consistency**\n1. Add `package.json` license field to `rhea-atlas/`:\n   ```json\n   \"license\": \"MIT\"\n   ```\n\n2. Create Python package metadata (choose one):\n   - Option A: Add `setup.py` with `license=\"MIT\"`\n   - Option B: Add `pyproject.toml` with `license = {text = \"MIT\"}`\n\n3. Update `rhea-atlas/README.md`:\n   - Replace \"Sovereign Logic\" with formal license declaration\n   - Add SPDX identifier: `<!-- License: MIT -->`\n\n#### **Phase 3: Documentation**\nUpdate `/docs/TERMS.md` Section 6:\n```markdown\n- **Platform code**: Open source under MIT License\n  See LICENSE file in repository root: https://github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project/blob/main/LICENSE\n```\n\n#### **Phase 4: Submodule Attribution**\nCreate `/NOTICE` at root listing:\n- Rhea Project core: MIT (2026)\n- Upstream Swift: Pow, SwiftUIX, Chat, etc. (each MIT)\n- Upstream Python: fastapi (BSD), google-auth (Apache), etc.\n- Upstream Node: next (Apache), three.js (MIT), etc.\n\n---\n\n### SUMMARY TABLE\n\n| Module | Status | License | Needs Action |\n|--------|--------|---------|--------------|\n| **ios/rhea-plus-ui/** | ✅ Complete | MIT | None |\n| **ios/RheaApp/** | ⚠️ Implicit | (MIT/Apache) | Add project.yml comment |\n| **rhea-atlas/** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Add LICENSE, update package.json |\n| **src/** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Add LICENSE or setup.py |\n| **contracts/** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Add LICENSE or setup.py |\n| **friends/aletheia/** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Add LICENSE |\n| **friends/ruliad/** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Add LICENSE |\n| **Root (repo)** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Create root LICENSE |\n| **All other modules** | ❌ CRITICAL | Undefined | Inherit from root |\n\n**Bottom Line:** Rhea has a single MIT license declaration (rhea-plus-ui), strong upstream MIT compatibility, but **missing formal root declaration and submodule consistency.** This creates legal ambiguity for users and violates npm/Python packaging standards."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a54aec213349f5813 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 79182\ntool_uses: 38\nduration_ms: 163888</usage>"}]}]},"uuid":"a1cfcd53-81d9-4fef-be4b-3101bccca1d9","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:27:10.924Z","toolUseResult":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to audit ALL licenses in the Rhea project at /Users/sa/rh.1. Specifically:\n\n1. Check every LICENSE, LICENSE.md, LICENSE.txt file in the entire repo tree\n2. Check all Package.swift files for dependency licenses\n3. Check these specific paths for license info:\n   - friends/aletheia/ (Aletheia module)\n   - friends/ruliad/ (Ruliad module)\n   - rhea-ontology-explorer/ (Ontology Explorer)\n   - rhea-atlas/ (Atlas frontend)\n   - src/ (core Python modules)\n   - ios/ (iOS app and packages)\n   - any other module directories\n\n4. Check package.json files for license fields\n5. Check pyproject.toml or setup.py for license info\n6. Look for any NOTICE files\n\nReturn a complete inventory: which modules have licenses, whi