{"parentUuid":"761a351f-8121-4995-a4b1-e7e319e88518","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011uR72ndJMY3fqqXj2TKQKH","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/sa/rh.1/docs/TERMS.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"88dadb12-d202-4ff9-93dd-8dde9d605aff","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:34:09.734Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/sa/rh.1/docs/TERMS.md","oldString":"- **Platform code**: open source under the license in the GitHub repository (github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project).","newString":"- **Platform code**: open source under the MIT License. See [LICENSE](https://github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project/blob/main/LICENSE).","originalFile":"# Terms of Service\n\n**Rhea Research Platform**\nTimeLabs NPO\nLast updated: 2026-02-26\n\n---\n\n## 1. Acceptance\n\nBy accessing or using the Rhea platform, you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the platform.\n\nRhea is operated by **TimeLabs NPO**, a non-profit organization focused on scientific research in chronobiology and related disciplines.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What Rhea Is\n\nRhea is a multi-model AI advisory system designed to assist researchers, scientists, and curious individuals. It is a **research tool**, not a medical device, clinical instrument, or licensed professional service.\n\nOutputs from Rhea are **informational only**. They do not constitute medical advice, legal advice, financial advice, or any other regulated professional guidance.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Permitted Use\n\nYou may use Rhea to:\n- Conduct scientific research and analysis\n- Explore hypotheses in chronobiology, pharmacology, and adjacent fields\n- Query AI models for literature synthesis, protocol design, and data interpretation\n- Share outputs for academic, educational, or non-commercial purposes\n\n**Fair use is expected.** You agree not to:\n- Use Rhea to generate disinformation, harassment, or harmful content\n- Attempt to reverse-engineer, scrape, or abuse the platform's infrastructure\n- Violate any applicable local, national, or international law\n- Impersonate researchers, institutions, or other users\n- Use automated bots or scripts against the platform without written permission\n\n---\n\n## 4. No Warranties\n\nRhea is provided **\"as is\"** and **\"as available\"**.\n\nTimeLabs NPO makes no warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to:\n- Accuracy or completeness of AI-generated content\n- Fitness for any particular scientific or clinical purpose\n- Uninterrupted or error-free availability\n- Compatibility with your systems or workflows\n\nAI models can hallucinate, make errors, or produce outdated information. Always verify outputs against authoritative sources. **Do not rely on Rhea outputs for clinical or safety-critical decisions.**\n\n---\n\n## 5. Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, TimeLabs NPO and its contributors shall not be liable for:\n- Any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from platform use\n- Errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in AI-generated content\n- Decisions made based on platform outputs\n- Data loss, service interruption, or unauthorized access events\n\n---\n\n## 6. Intellectual Property\n\n- **Your inputs and research**: remain yours. TimeLabs NPO does not claim ownership of queries you submit.\n- **Platform code**: open source under the license in the GitHub repository (github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project).\n- **AI model outputs**: governed by the terms of the underlying model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.).\n\n---\n\n## 7. Open Source and Contributions\n\nRhea's source code is publicly available at **github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project**. Contributions are welcome under the repository's contributing guidelines. By submitting a pull request or contribution, you agree that your contribution may be incorporated under the project's open-source license.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Accounts and Access\n\nIf Rhea offers account creation in the future:\n- You are responsible for maintaining the security of your credentials\n- You must not share accounts or allow unauthorized access\n- TimeLabs NPO reserves the right to suspend accounts that violate these Terms\n\n---\n\n## 9. Changes to These Terms\n\nTimeLabs NPO may update these Terms. Changes will be posted in this file with an updated date and noted in the repository changelog. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Governing Law\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction where TimeLabs NPO is established. Disputes shall be resolved in good faith first; escalation proceeds under applicable law.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Contact\n\nQuestions about these Terms:\n**celestica201@gmail.com**\nGitHub: github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":66,"oldLines":7,"newStart":66,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ## 6. Intellectual Property"," "," - **Your inputs and research**: remain yours. TimeLabs NPO does not claim ownership of queries you submit.","-- **Platform code**: open source under the license in the GitHub repository (github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project).","+- **Platform code**: open source under the MIT License. See [LICENSE](https://github.com/serg-alexv/rhea-project/blob/main/LICENSE)."," - **AI model outputs**: governed by the terms of the underlying model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, etc.)."," "," ---"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"761a351f-8121-4995-a4b1-e7e319e88518"}
