{"parentUuid":"93595a52-be24-4fb2-aaf4-9ecb37a7cf41","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EkMDxMQongRgFPG5F9obz1","type":"tool_result","content":"sa               64353   0.0  0.0 427989888    112   ??  Ss    1:03PM   0:02.04 /Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Volumes/iOS_23C54/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Profiles/Runtimes/iOS 26.2.simruntime/Contents/Resources/RuntimeRoot/Applications/Passbook.app/PlugIns/PassbookWidgetsExtension-iPhone.appex/PassbookWidgetsExtension-iPhone -LaunchArguments REDACTED","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"03fe0b91-991c-4cb7-8a39-d29cbdf1d929","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:49:05.292Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"sa               64353   0.0  0.0 427989888    112   ??  Ss    1:03PM   0:02.04 /Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Volumes/iOS_23C54/Library/Developer/CoreSimulator/Profiles/Runtimes/iOS 26.2.simruntime/Contents/Resources/RuntimeRoot/Applications/Passbook.app/PlugIns/PassbookWidgetsExtension-iPhone.appex/PassbookWidgetsExtension-iPhone -LaunchArguments REDACTED","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"93595a52-be24-4fb2-aaf4-9ecb37a7cf41"}
{"parentUuid":"03fe0b91-991c-4cb7-8a39-d29cbdf1d929","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BYK6U4GhovLPo752mrdsxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No `cliclick`, no `pyautogui`, no `xdotool`. iPhone Mirroring isn't running (only iOS Simulator processes). \n\nBut we can install `cliclick` via homebrew, or use AppleScript's `do shell script \"...\"` + `CGEvent` approach. Or install pyautogui via pip.\n\nActually, the simplest approach without installing anything: use AppleScript + `osascript` to control the cursor. macOS has built-in cursor control via Accessibility APIs that can be invoked via `osascript`.\n\nBut the user's real proposal is more interesting: build a component INSIDE the Rhea app that can receive remote tap commands. \n\nThe better approach is to build a remote control agent directly in the iOS app. I'd add a `/remote/tap` endpoint to the API that accepts tap coordinates and actions, plus a `/remote/screen` endpoint that streams screenshots back. Then in the iOS app itself, I can create a view that listens for these remote commands and translates them into actual touches on the screen.\n\nBut here's the catch—iOS apps can only interact with their own views, not other apps like Play. The real solution would be either using iOS Shortcuts to automate Play's workflows through URL schemes, or stepping back and using `cliclick` with iPhone Mirroring on macOS to simulate taps at the system level.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the user might want something more creative: what if I build a component within the Rhea app itself that acts as my remote interface? I could embed a WKWebView that loads Play's web interface if it exists, then send JavaScript commands or tap events directly to that WebView—essentially giving me a way to interact with Play's content from within the Rhea app's sandbox.\n\nBut Play doesn't have a web interface, so that won't work. Let me refocus on what the user actually needs: exporting all Play components. The simplest approach would be to use `cliclick` on the Mac side—start iPhone Mirroring, take screenshots, find the Play app, and navigate through it programmatically to export everything.\n\nThough the user specifically asked to build something for the Rhea app and said they're open to experimenting. So maybe the real proposal is a lightweight remote-control bridge in Rhea that captures the screen using ReplayKit...\n\nActually, I'm overthinking this. The user said \"don't ask questions\"—they want a practical solution. Mac-side automation with cliclick is the most straightforward path forward.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2754,"cache_read_input_tokens":153167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2754},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYaoxzapaWggPW7YcoX4S","type":"assistant","uuid":"317ed63a-c8aa-484d-8e81-0d0d54ed903c","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:50:09.650Z"}
{"parentUuid":"317ed63a-c8aa-484d-8e81-0d0d54ed903c","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BYK6U4GhovLPo752mrdsxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Понял идею. Два пути к одной цели — давай оба параллельно:\n\n**Сейчас (Mac-side, работает за 2 минуты):**\n`screencapture` + `cliclick` → клики на iPhone Mirroring окне → управляю Play.app через зеркало.\n\n**Эксперимент (iOS компонент):**\n`RemoteControlView` в Rhea app — принимает команды через API, показывает куда тапнуть, captures screen обратно.\n\nСтавлю `cliclick` и делаю скрипт-мост:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2754,"cache_read_input_tokens":153167,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2754},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYaoxzapaWggPW7YcoX4S","type":"assistant","uuid":"73fb6131-2aaa-4c53-bbe4-fd64431a3a6a","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:50:12.804Z"}
{"parentUuid":"73fb6131-2aaa-4c53-bbe4-fd64431a3a6a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BYK6U4GhovLPo752mrdsxz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HcGXTA5zNtZoZFMgz3NiUc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"brew install cliclick 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Install cliclick for cursor automation","timeout":60000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2754,"cache_read_input_tokens":153167,"output_tokens":1337,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2754,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CYaoxzapaWggPW7YcoX4S","type":"assistant","uuid":"f69bfc31-16a1-453b-a861-ec1e15a264ac","timestamp":"2026-02-28T16:50:14.178Z"}
