{"parentUuid":"9dacb0f0-ad39-4b49-8f26-c699e86e75d9","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PhpJScoEc3j6er6rCTP1DN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The mirroring window still looks the same - the swipe didn't seem to work. The phone screen is still showing the home screen with the wallpaper. \n\nI notice the Rhea Radio widget at the top right now shows: \"ndi ndi_abird| ndi/wavem | procn=2 | ndi_procn=1 | ndi_ports=0 | recent_capture=0\"\n\nThe issue might be that:\n1. The iPhone Mirroring window needs to be clicked/focused first before input is accepted\n2. The cliclick coordinates might not be mapping correctly to the mirrored content\n3. The mirroring window might have a toolbar or border that offsets the content\n\n\n4. The drag gesture might need a different approach - maybe cliclick's drag commands aren't properly simulating touch swipes on the mirrored display, so I should try typing directly to see if Spotlight is already open but just not visually apparent in the screenshot.\n\nLet me try using keyboard shortcuts instead since iPhone Mirroring supports keyboard input - I can either use Cmd+3 for the home screen or just try typing to search. I need to look more carefully at where the search bar actually is on the screen given the window dimensions and iPhone 13 Pro Max aspect ratio. .5:9), the phone screen in the window would be something like... Let me calculate. The window is 444 wide. The phone content area might be padded within that.\n\nLet me just try clicking at different coordinates more carefully. The search bar text \"Q Search\" appears to be at roughly the bottom 5% of the phone screen. If the content area is from y=60 (below title bar) to y=1003 (bottom), then the search bar would be around y=980.\n\nBut wait, I see that the window height is 972 from y=31, so the bottom of the window is at y=31+972=1003. The search bar should be near y ≈ 990-1000.\n\nLet me try y=990.\n\nActually, maybe I should try a completely different approach. Let me try using the keyboard. If I click on the mirroring window and then just start typing or use Cmd+Space, it might trigger search on the phone. Though in iPhone Mirroring, I think I just need to click somewhere to focus a text field first.\n\nLet me try a cleaner approach instead—maybe I should capture just the iPhone Mirroring window to get precise coordinates, or try swiping down more aggressively, or clicking directly on the \"Search\" text.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":92801,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYarJUkVTvkHK2PSfs6uk","type":"assistant","uuid":"c103815d-847c-4353-bfd0-9c148411bd01","timestamp":"2026-02-28T17:20:44.506Z"}
