{"parentUuid":"91a125ac-78fd-4e18-a1b9-b524a233d0ff","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/sa/rh.1","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","version":"2.1.59","gitBranch":"stage4-release","slug":"snazzy-skipping-brook","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01KURtfD45fQZxPqPWctWYUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"No ATS exception at all! That means:1. `http://localhost:8400` is blocked by ATS on device (HTTP not allowed)\n2. `localhost` resolves to the phone itself, not the Mac\n\nI need to:\n1. Add `NSAppTransportSecurity` with `NSAllowsArbitraryLoads` to Info.plist (or better, add `NSAllowsLocalNetworking`)\n2. Make the default URL work for local development\n\nFor production, the API should be behind HTTPS. But for local dev/TestFlight testing, we need to allow local network HTTP.\n\n\nI should add `NSAllowsLocalNetworking = true` to Info.plist to permit HTTP on the local network, then handle the different scenarios: localhost works on the simulator, but on a real device I'll need the Mac's local IP address, and for remote testing I'd need something like ngrok or Cloud Run.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":703,"cache_read_input_tokens":138741,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":703},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYatLwSPYAEt6UCsYYYjH","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f597417-64dc-4a77-99cf-c2f06ecbe7b5","timestamp":"2026-02-28T17:47:17.813Z"}
