{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-02-28T18:07:54.729Z","sessionId":"94aabe90-9b2d-48e7-be8c-6bf820a0b6a9","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a88c01984ac501b4c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Find available API keys\" completed</summary>\n<result>Perfect! Now let me create a summary document:\n\n## API Key Audit Complete — Summary Report\n\nI've completed a comprehensive search for LLM API keys available to the Rhea project. Here are the findings:\n\n### KEY DISCOVERY RESULTS\n\n**Working Keys Found: 1**\n\n1. **GEMINI_API_KEY** (Google AI Studio) — VALID & TESTED\n   - Location: `/Users/sa/rh.1/.env`\n   - Prefix: `AIzaSyA72p...` (39 characters)\n   - Status: ✓ Successfully connected to gemini-2.5-flash model\n   - This is a free Google AI Studio API key\n\n2. **FIREBASE_API_KEY** (Google Firebase) — PRESENT\n   - Location: `/Users/sa/rh.1/.env`\n   - Prefix: `AIzaSyAE7T...` (39 characters)\n   - Status: Present and validated (different purpose from LLM)\n\n### MISSING KEYS (Not Configured)\n\nThe following LLM providers have no keys configured:\n- **OpenAI** (OPENAI_API_KEY) — no key set\n- **Anthropic** (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) — no key set\n- **DeepSeek** (DEEPSEEK_API_KEY) — no key set\n- **OpenRouter** (OPENROUTER_API_KEY) — no key set\n- **HuggingFace** (HF_TOKEN) — no key set\n- **Azure** (AZURE_API_KEY) — no key set\n\n### STORAGE LOCATIONS VERIFIED\n\n- ✓ `/Users/sa/rh.1/.env` — Contains Gemini and Firebase keys\n- ✓ `/Users/sa/rh.1/.env.example` — Template exists\n- ✗ `/Users/sa/.env` — Does not exist\n- ✗ `~/.claude/settings.local.json` — No env keys configured\n- ✗ macOS Keychain — No matching API key entries\n- ✓ Environment variables — GEMINI_API_KEY loaded in shell\n\n### RHEA BRIDGE STATUS\n\nThe bridge at `src/rhea_bridge.py` shows:\n- **Total Providers**: 7 configured\n- **Available**: 1 (Gemini only)\n- **Total Models in Bridge**: 34+\n- Command: `python3 src/rhea_bridge.py status` returns full provider JSON\n\n### LOCALHOST:8400 READINESS\n\n**Current Status**: Limited (Gemini only)\n- Can query: `gemini-2.5-flash`, `gemini-2.5-pro`, `gemini-2.0-flash`\n- Cannot query: GPT-4, Claude, DeepSeek, HuggingFace models\n\n### KEY MANAGEMENT INFRASTRUCTURE\n\n**Excellent**: The project has a secure key rotation script at `/Users/sa/rh.1/scripts/rhea/rotate_key.sh` with features:\n- Safe clipboard-based key insertion (never in shell history)\n- Auto-create capability for Gemini\n- Audit, test, and wipe commands\n- Supports all 8 providers (openai, anthropic, gemini, openrouter, deepseek, hf, azure, firebase)\n\n### IMMEDIATE ACTION NEEDED\n\nTo support localhost:8400 with multiple providers, you need to:\n\n1. Create additional API keys from provider consoles\n2. Use the safe rotation script: `bash scripts/rhea/rotate_key.sh paste <provider>`\n3. Test with: `bash scripts/rhea/rotate_key.sh test`\n\nThe infrastructure is ready; only keys are missing.</result>\n<usage><total_tokens>72848</total_tokens><tool_uses>23</tool_uses><duration_ms>178682</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\nFull transcript available at: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-sa-rh-1/tasks/a88c01984ac501b4c.output"}
